 To create a new calendar event for the hiking trip with Mark, you can use the `create_calendar_event` function. Here's an example of how you could call this function:

```json
{
  "name": "create_hiking_trip_event",
  "arguments": {
    "title": "Hiking Trip with Mark",
    "start_time": "2023-04-15 10:00",
    "end_time": "2023-04-15 15:00",
    "location": "Grand Canyon, Arizona",
    "participants": ["mark@example.com"]
  }
}
```

In this example, the event title is set to "Hiking Trip with Mark". The start time and end time are set for April 15th, 2023, from 10:00 AM to 3:00 PM (5 hours). The location is set to "Grand Canyon, Arizona", which should be the location mentioned in the email. Lastly, Mark's email address is added as a participant.

You can modify this example according to the specific details from the emails you have received about the hiking trip. After creating the function, you can call it using the following command:

```json
{
  "name": "create_hiking_trip_event"
}
```
